---
import HeroFilm from "./HeroFilm.astro";
---

<figure class="overview-stage hero-story-stage" aria-label="How Movcues turns user behavior into contextual onboarding">
  <HeroFilm />
  <figcaption class="story-caption" id="hero-film-caption">
    <strong>One workflow, from insight to action.</strong>
    Find onboarding drop-offs with <a href="/product/analytics">behavior analytics</a>,
    segment users by their actions, deliver <a href="/product/experiences">contextual experiences</a>,
    and evaluate completion to decide what to improve next.
  </figcaption>
  <details class="story-transcript">
    <summary>Read the video walkthrough</summary>
    <p><strong>0:00 — Find the friction.</strong> Users sign up. But where do they stop?</p>
    <p><strong>0:02.8 — Understand behavior.</strong> An illustrative funnel shows 1,000 sign-ups, 620 users starting setup, and 340 creating a project. Of those starting setup, 280 do not complete it: a 45% drop-off.</p>
    <p><strong>0:06.4 — Target the right audience.</strong> The team configures an audience for users who triggered setup_started but not project_created. The example audience contains 280 matching users.</p>
    <p><strong>0:09.8 — Guide users in context.</strong> In Acme Workspace, an anchored tooltip prompts the user to create their first project. They select the call to action and create the Website launch project.</p>
    <p><strong>0:15 — Evaluate completion.</strong> Experience reporting shows 120 views and 78 completions, a 65% completion rate. Use these findings to decide what to improve next.</p>
    <p><strong>0:18 — Turn user behavior into action.</strong> Understand. Target. Guide. Improve.</p>
    <p class="transcript-note">The video uses illustrative interfaces and example data.</p>
  </details>
</figure>

